=== layout: title-content

# Genetic Palindromes

@body

- A palindromic sequence is one where the 5&prime; to 3&prime; sequence is identical on both strands of a double strand polynucleotide
- 5&prime;-`AGTACT`-3&prime;
- 3&prime;-`TCATGA`-5&prime;
- all the base pairs match

=== layout: title-content

# Base Pair from Front to Back

@body

- 5&prime;-`AGTACT`-3&prime;

=== layout: title-content

# Base Pair from Front to Back

@body

- A-T pair
- T-A pair
- 5&prime;-`AGTACT`-3&prime;
- 5&prime;-`AGTACT`-3&prime;
- YES, it’s a
- palindrome
- 3&prime;-`TCATGA`-3&prime;
- G-C pair

=== layout: title-content

# Base Pair from Front to Back

@body

- A-T pair
- T-G pair
- 5&prime;-`AGTGCT`-3&prime;
- 5&prime;-`AGTGCT`-3&prime;
- NO, it’s not a
- palindrome
- 3&prime;-`TCGTGA`-3&prime;
- G-C pair

=== layout: title-content

# Base Pair from Front to Back

@body

- you cannot have
- an odd number of
- nucleotides in a
- genetic palindrome
- A-T pair
- T-A pair
- 5&prime;-`AGTGACT`-3&prime;
- central
- unpaired
- 5&prime;-`AGTGACT`-3&prime;
- NO, it’s not a
- palindrome
- G-C pair
- 3&prime;-`TCAGTGA`-3&prime;

=== layout: title-only

# Restriction Enzymes

=== layout: title-content

# Restriction enzymes cleave DNA at a specific sequence

@body

![Slide image 8](assets/lect02e-restriction_enzymes/image_008.jpg)

=== layout: two-panels

# Restriction enzymes

@left

![Slide image 9](assets/lect02e-restriction_enzymes/image_009.png)

@right

- The DNA recognition sequence is usually a 4-6 bp palindrome
- Restriction enzymes are named after the organisms from which they were isolated
- The cuts may result in blunt or sticky ends
- Sticky ends may have 5&prime; or 3&prime;-overhangs

=== layout: title-content

# Slide 31

@body

![Slide image 10](assets/lect02e-restriction_enzymes/image_010.png)

=== layout: title-content

# Slide 32

@body

![Slide image 11](assets/lect02e-restriction_enzymes/image_011.png)

=== layout: title-content

# Restriction enzymes and their recognition sites

@body

- HaeIII | Haemophilus aegiptius | `GG/CC` | Blunt cut
- Sau3A | Staphylococcus aureus | /`GATC` | 5&prime;-overhang
- HhaI | Haemophilus haemolyticus | `GCG/C` | 3&prime;-overhang
- SmaI | Serratia marcescens | CCC / GGG | Blunt cut
- EcoRI | Escherichia coli RY13 | G / `AATTC` | 5&prime;-overhang
- PstI | Providencia Stuartii | `CTGCA` / G | 3&prime;-overhang
- HaeII | Haemophilus aegiptius | RGCGC / Y | Ambiguous sequence
- NotI | Nocardia otitidis | GC / `GGCCGC` | 8 nt sequence

